※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4922 LANG_OPERATOR_ARITY

※ An operator is written before one operand or between two, so a definition of
※ one takes one parameter or two.  Which of the two it is, is what tells a
※ prefix reading from an infix one where a glyph has both, so the number is not
※ something a definition may leave for a reader to work out.

type Point = x : u8 ; y : u8

fn `⊛`(a: Point, b: Point, c: Point) → Point:
    a

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    0u6
